\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces Direct metallicity against \def ##1{##1}\cite  {izotov_2018} strong line proxy determined for 21 of 38 pea candidates; parametric estimations described in green, while direct electron temperature calculation plotted in red. Note the separation of galaxies into three populations, and the strong correlation between the calibrated strong line metric and true metallicity at high ionisation. Note further the bias for the parametric method's use against preferentially lower R23 candidates; this is a selection effect given that lower R23-O32 indicates a smaller [OIII] emission flux: these objects are likely of preferentially smaller SNR and therefore smaller auroral flux. Corresponding low- and high- metallicity spectra plotted for comparison.}}{8}{figure.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mcities}{{11}{8}{Direct metallicity against \cite {izotov_2018} strong line proxy determined for 21 of 38 pea candidates; parametric estimations described in green, while direct electron temperature calculation plotted in red. Note the separation of galaxies into three populations, and the strong correlation between the calibrated strong line metric and true metallicity at high ionisation. Note further the bias for the parametric method's use against preferentially lower R23 candidates; this is a selection effect given that lower R23-O32 indicates a smaller [OIII] emission flux: these objects are likely of preferentially smaller SNR and therefore smaller auroral flux. Corresponding low- and high- metallicity spectra plotted for comparison}{figure.caption.11}{}}
