\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces IR emission versus [OIII] flux and equivalent width for green pea candidates for Spitzer IRCam channels 1 and 2. The upper panel shows proportional channel flux with corresponding metallicities plotted while the lower panel shows individual band fluxes. Note the difference in rate of change of IR flux across bands due to 4.6 micron emission dominated by nebular emission from highly star forming galaxies. Right hand pane shows BPT-style IR colour vs normalised [OIII] emission plot, isolating four dusty torus-candidate green peas.}}{10}{figure.caption.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:spitzer}{{13}{10}{IR emission versus [OIII] flux and equivalent width for green pea candidates for Spitzer IRCam channels 1 and 2. The upper panel shows proportional channel flux with corresponding metallicities plotted while the lower panel shows individual band fluxes. Note the difference in rate of change of IR flux across bands due to 4.6 micron emission dominated by nebular emission from highly star forming galaxies. Right hand pane shows BPT-style IR colour vs normalised [OIII] emission plot, isolating four dusty torus-candidate green peas}{figure.caption.13}{}}
